                <pb facs="0985" n="849" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg849"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/525: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Morgan</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-05-20T18:00:00-04:00">May 20, 1929—6
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>17. Department’s 15, May 11, 6 p.m.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d705-f1"/> The
                    Commission of Inquiry and Conciliation has arranged for the repatriation of
                    prisoners held respectively by Bolivia and Paraguay. The prisoners held by
                    Paraguay will be brought to Corumbá, if the Brazilian Government consents to a
                    request already made through the Brazilian Embassy here for this purpose. When
                    Brazilian consent is received the Military Attaché at your Mission will be asked
                    to proceed with a Brazilian officer to Corumbá to assist in connection with the
                    repatriation. Further instructions will be sent for this purpose.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
